WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:05.299
Kevin Feige and his merry band of Marvel movie-makers
brought down the house at San Diego Comic-Con

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:06.299
2019.

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:11.250
To a sea of buzzing fans, Marvel Studios announced
a shining slate of Phase 4 movies and television

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.010
series set to launch over the next two years
everything from the Jane Foster-featuring

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.679
Thor: Love and Thunder to a Shang-Chi movie,
to a bunch of Disney+ superhero shows.

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:23.990
What was missing from the jam-packed panel,
though, was the announcement of another Avengers

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.019
movie which some fans were holding out hope
for, thanks to past rumors that suggested

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:32.369
Marvel was cooking up a fifth ensemble film
featuring Earth's Mightiest Heroes.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.851
In the aftermath of Marvel's presentation,
studio president Feige revealed to IGN the

00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:40.540
reason why Avengers 5 wasn't announced at
San Diego Comic-Con.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.330
Simply put, it's because there will be no
Avengers 5, as far as Feige is concerned.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:49.230
The era of Avengers films as we know them
concluded with Avengers: Endgame, Feige explained,

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.320
and it's now time for the Marvel Cinematic
Universe to move on to new superhero stories.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.910
It isn't necessarily out with the old, but
it's certainly in with the new when it comes

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.570
to Phase 4 of the MCU.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.570
Feige explained:

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.430
"We had a movie this year called Avengers:
Endgame, and it is very much an ending, as

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.540
you saw, to so many of those characters.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.100
So Phase 4 is about beginnings, and Phase
4 is about learning new things about characters

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.830
you already think you know like Black Widow,
meeting incredible new characters like The

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:18.930
Eternals and Shang-Chi, going on new adventures
with Doctor Strange and Thor, and these Disney+

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.100
shows, which I promise will be spectacular
and not what anybody's expecting."

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.620
Feige isn't saying that the past needs to
die and that Marvel should never acknowledge

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.640
the Avengers again, but it's clear he wants
Marvel fans to understand that the new chapter

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.110
of the MCU is meant to be just that: new.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:37.130
Though it's not easy to let go and say goodbye
to heroes you've watched evolve for years,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:41.090
and while it will take some time for everyone
to fully recover from the events of Avengers:

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:44.330
Endgame, there's really nothing to do but
give in to change right?

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.950
"Dread it.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.980
Run from it.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.840
Destiny arrives all the same.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.400
And now it's here."

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.850
OK, well, uhh… maybe that guy's not the
best guy to take philosophical advice from.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:02.100
Anyway, Earth's Mightiest Heroes very well
might round up again but it won't happen in

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.260
Phase 4.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.780
And the potential ensemble flick will feature
a different roster, likely a blend of older

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:12.090
Marvel mainstays and fresh faces introduced
in Phase 4 and the to-be-announced Phase 5.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.280
Longtime Marvel star Samuel L. Jackson is
confident of this possibility, and believes

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.680
that his character, Nick Fury, will round
up the villain-fighting forces in the future.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:25.410
Asked by CinemaBlend if he thinks that Avengers-centric
movies should be "shelved" in favor of team-up

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:30.040
films like Spider-Man: Far From Home, which
brought Fury and new MCU character Mysterio

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.160
into Spidey's solo series, Jackson said he
doesn't agree.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.150
He elaborated, saying that Fury knows a threat
is headed to Earth, and that he'll eventually

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.140
need to create a new crew of Avengers to defeat
the imminent danger.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.430
"I always think that there's room for every
kind of story to be told.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.989
And at some point, they're going to have to
put together another Avengers group of some

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:49.260
sorts to deal with whatever's coming next.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.440
Nick [Fury] knows something is coming, the
same way he found out in Captain Marvel that

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.380
there are other things that need to be dealt
with that [he] didn't know about.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.099
This is moving us to another place."

00:02:58.099 --> 00:03:00.050
So, could we get a Young Avengers movie?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.050
Maybe!

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.250
Perhaps a Dark Avengers film?

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.760
Yeah, why not?

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.560
But a fifth Avengers flick with the OG Thor
and Cap, Iron Man and Black Widow, Hawkeye

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.560
and Hulk?

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.130
Well… don't hold your breath.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.210
Unless you're Nick Fury.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.129
You never tell Nick Fury he's wrong…

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:17.100
"We get into a situation like this again,
what happens then?"

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.250
"They'll come back."

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.190
"You really sure about that?"

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.650
"I am."

